# Trivy ignore list — base-OS package CVEs with no upstream Debian fix yet.
#
# Every entry here was verified (docker/security.yml SCA scan, last checked
# 2026-08-31) to have no "Fixed Version" available in the Debian trixie
# repository — Trivy would flag these regardless of anything we change in
# this project, since they belong to packages pulled in by the
# `python:3.12-slim` base image itself, not anything we apt-install
# ourselves. None of these packages (gzip, libacl1, ncurses, sqlite3, perl)
# are invoked by RequestTrace at runtime.
#
# Review policy: re-run the container-scan job without this file
# periodically (the weekly scheduled run already does the real scan) and
# remove an entry as soon as its CVE shows a Fixed Version.

# gzip — LZH decompression buffer overflow; gzip is never invoked by RequestTrace.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 — symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl functions.
CVE-2026-54369

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) — buffer overflow.
CVE-2025-69720

# libsqlite3-0 — FTS5 full-text-search arbitrary code execution / crash.
# Python's sqlite3 stdlib module links this, but RequestTrace never uses it.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# perl-base and bundled perl modules — RequestTrace never invokes perl;
# these ship as part of the Debian base image's essential package set.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-9538
